    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:36+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:36+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of WA extends a ridge over southern parts of the state while a weak trough lies across central Australia near the norther border. The high will drift over the southeast today and into the Tasman Sea on Friday, allowing a trough and low pressure system to move across SA on Friday. A brief high pressure system settles over SA on Saturday before another trough and low starts to move across from WA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Daytime maximum temperatures 24 to 29.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm from the late morning. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h increasing to 35 km/h before tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 23 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds north to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. The chance of morning fog west of the ranges. Slight chance of a shower, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the evening. Light winds becoming northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 32.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
